  {
    "title": "ě sounds like “ye” in “yet” (or plain “e”)",
    "body": "The ideal sound is “ye” as in “yet”, with the consonant before it slightly softened: dělo is close to “DYE-lo”. A plain “e”, as South Slavs say it, is also understood. Pick one and use it consistently.",
    "pattern": "ě",
    "examples": [
      {
        "word": "lět",
        "say": "lyet",
        "en": "years (of age)"
      },
      {
        "word": "děti",
        "say": "DYE-tee",
        "en": "children"
      },
